Specification Types

# Add additional types here to show how they work 

Scenario Use the attributes in different order 
Given type values are  : SomeTypes
| anInt | aDouble | aChar | achar1 |
| 0     | 0.0     | x     | y      |
| 111   | 222.2   | q     |        |
Then this should be equal : SomeTypes
# Note the order is changed just to show order is independent
| achar1 | anInt | aDouble | aChar |
| y      | 0     | 0.0     | x     |
|        | 111   | 222.2   | q     |

Scenario Use the default values for attributes
Given type values are  : SomeTypes
| anInt | aChar |
| 0     | x     |
Then this should be equal : SomeTypes
# Note the order is changed just to show order is independent
| achar1 | anInt | aDouble | aChar |
| y      | 0     | 0.0     | x     |



Attributes SomeTypes
Description Some types to try out
| Name    | Default | DataType  | Notes |
| anInt   | 0       | Integer   |       |
| aDouble | 0.0     | Float     |       |
| aChar   | q       | Character |       |
| achar1  | y       | Character |       |

DataType AccountType
Description Allowed account categories.
Details \
  These are the only valid account types in this system. 
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value    | Notes                    |
| Checking | Standard demand deposit  |
| Savings  | Interest-bearing deposit |

DataType Dollar
Description Monetary amount in US dollars.
Details \
  Stored as decimal with two digits of precision. 
Constraint Must not have more than two decimal digits.
Examples: ValidValues
| Value | IsValid | Notes                 |
| 0     | true    |                       |
| 0.01  | true    |                       |
| -1    | false   | Negative not allowed  |
| 0.001 | false   | Only 2 decimal digits |


DomainTerm WithdrawalAmount : Dollar
Description The amount of money a customer requests to withdraw.
Constraint Must be greater than zero.

DataType SimpleText 
Description Allows alphabetic, numeric, space, hyphen, period, comma 
Examples: ValidValues
| Value      | IsValid | Notes       |
| abc        | y       |             |
| ab.        | y       | period okay |
| 1234567890 | y       | digits      |
| @          | n       |             |
| -a-b       | y       | hyphens     |
